/* REFERENCE SNAPSHOT — NOT a compile target. Do not #import this.
 *
 * Full ObjC class dump of the Apple private Safari.framework, kept for diffing
 * against future macOS/Safari versions. The compile-ready, hand-curated header
 * we actually build against is SafariPrivateFramework.h.
 *
 *   Framework version : 625.2.8.11.9
 *   macOS / hardware   : 27.2 (build 26B118), Apple M4 (arm64e)
 *   Dumped            : 2026-10-24
 *
 * How it was made (the old recipe in SafariPrivateFramework.h no longer works:
 * since macOS 11 the framework binary is not a file on disk — it lives in the
 * dyld shared cache, and Safari is in a Cryptex; the 2013 class-dump 3.5 can't
 * read arm64e). Using Blacktop's ipsw (https://github.com/blacktop/ipsw):
 *
 *   ipsw dyld macho --objc \
 *     /System/Volumes/Preboot/Cryptexes/OS/System/Library/dyld/dyld_shared_cache_arm64e \
 *     /System/Library/PrivateFrameworks/Safari.framework/Versions/A/Safari
 *
 * NOTE: `ipsw --objc` emits selectors + property type-encodings but NOT
 * fully-typed method signatures (methods appear as `-[Class selector:];`). To
 * regenerate a typed, compile-ready header, extract the dylib (`ipsw dyld macho
 * -x ...`) and run an arm64e-capable class-dump fork.
 */

